\fs96 \cf2 Testing\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf12 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf12 \cb13 Caution\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa127\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb13 The 
\fs24\fsmilli12250 \cf10 \cb14 mojo test
\fs28 \cf2 \cb13  command was removed as of October 31, 2025. For more information, see the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/modular/modular/blob/modular/v26.2/mojo/proposals/mojo-test-deprecation.md"}}{\fldrslt \ul deprecation proposal}} and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://forum.modular.com/t/proposal-deprecating-mojo-test/2371"}}{\fldrslt \ul forum announcement}}.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb13 The recommended approach for testing is now to use the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/suite/TestSuite/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs24\fsmilli12250 \cb14 \ul TestSuite}} struct from the standard library, which provides automatic test discovery and execution. Continue reading for current testing instructions using 
\fs24\fsmilli12250 \cf10 \cb14 TestSuite
\fs28 \cf2 \cb13 .\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Mojo includes a framework for developing and executing unit tests. The Mojo testing framework consists of a set of assertions defined as part of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/lib/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 Mojo standard library}} and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/suite/TestSuite/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 \ul \ulc5 TestSuite}} struct for automatic test discovery and execution.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa800\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 Get started\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Let's start with a simple example of writing and running Mojo tests.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 1. Write tests\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 For your first example of using the Mojo testing framework, create a file named 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 test_quickstart.mojo
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  containing the following code:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf6 \cb16 # Content of test_quickstart.mojo\cf17 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb16 from\cf17  std\cf5 .\cf17 testing \cf5 import\cf17  assert_equal\cf5 ,\cf17  TestSuite\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 def\cf17  \cf18 inc\cf5 (\cf17 n\cf5 :\cf17  Int\cf5 )\cf17  raises \cf5 ->\cf17  Int\cf5 :\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     \cf5 return\cf17  n \cf5 +\cf17  \cf19 1\cf17 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 def\cf17  \cf18 test_inc_zero\cf5 ()\cf17  raises\cf5 :\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     \cf6 # This test contains an intentional logical error to show an example of\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     \cf6 # what a test failure looks like at runtime.\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     assert_equal\cf5 (\cf17 inc\cf5 (\cf19 0\cf5 ),\cf17  \cf19 0\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 def\cf17  \cf18 test_inc_one\cf5 ()\cf17  raises\cf5 :\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     assert_equal\cf5 (\cf17 inc\cf5 (\cf19 1\cf5 ),\cf17  \cf19 2\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 def\cf17  \cf18 main\cf5 ()\cf17  raises\cf5 :\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     TestSuite\cf5 .\cf17 discover_tests\cf5 [\cf17 __functions_in_module\cf5 ()]().\cf17 run\cf5 ()\cf17 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf20 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf21 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 In this file, the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 inc()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  function is the test target. The functions whose names begin with 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 test_
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  are the tests. Usually you should define the target in a separate source file from its tests, but you can define them in the same file for this simple example.\
A test function fails if it raises an error when executed, otherwise it passes. The two tests in this example use the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 assert_equal()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  function, which raises an error if the two values provided are not equal.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 \cb22 The implementation of 
\fs24\fsmilli12250 \cf10 \cb14 test_inc_zero()
\fs28 \cf2 \cb22  contains an intentional logical error so that you can see an example of a failed test when you execute it in the next step of this tutorial.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 2. Execute tests\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Then in the directory containing the file, execute the following command in your shell:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf17 \cb16 mojo run test_quickstart.mojo\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf20 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf21 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 You should see output similar to this (note that this example elides the full filesystem paths from the output shown):\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf17 \cb16 Unhandled exception caught during execution:\cb1 \
\cb16 Running 2 tests for ROOT_DIR/test_quickstart.mojo\cb1 \
\cb16     FAIL [ 0.009 ] test_inc_zero\cb1 \
\cb16       At ROOT_DIR/test_quickstart.mojo:40:5: AssertionError: `left == right` comparison failed:\cb1 \
\cb16          left: 1\cb1 \
\cb16         right: 0\cb1 \
\cb16     PASS [ 0.001 ] test_inc_one\cb1 \
\cb16 --------\cb1 \
\cb16 Summary [ 0.009 ] 2 tests run: 1 passed , 1 failed , 0 skipped\cb1 \
\cb16 Test suite 'ROOT_DIR/test_quickstart.mojo' failed!\cb1 \
\
\cb16 mojo: error: execution exited with a non-zero result: 1\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The output shows each test as it runs with PASS or FAIL status and execution time, followed by a summary of tests run, passed, failed, and skipped. Failed tests display their error messages inline.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Next steps\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Using Mojo assertion functions\cf2 \ulnone  describes the assertion functions available to help implement tests.\
\ls4\ilvl0\cf5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Writing unit tests\cf2 \ulnone  shows how to write unit tests and organize them into test files.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Our GitHub repo contains an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/modular/modular/tree/modular/v26.2/mojo/examples/testing"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 example project}} to demonstrate unit testing. Several of the examples shown later are based on this project.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa800\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 Using Mojo assertion functions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The Mojo standard library includes a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/testing/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 \ul \ulc5 testing}} module that defines several assertion functions for implementing tests. Each assertion returns 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 None
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  if its condition is met or raises an error if it isn't.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/testing/assert_true/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul assert_true()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Asserts that the input value is 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/testing/assert_false/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul assert_false()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Asserts that the input value is 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 False
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/testing/assert_equal/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul assert_equal()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Asserts that the input values are equal.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/testing/assert_not_equal/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul assert_not_equal()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Asserts that the input values are not equal.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/testing/assert_almost_equal/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul assert_almost_equal()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Asserts that the input values are equal up to a tolerance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The boolean assertions report a basic error message when they fail.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb16 from\cf17  std\cf5 .\cf17 testing \cf5 import\cf17  \cf5 *\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16 assert_true\cf5 (\cf19 False\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf20 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf21 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf17 \cb16 Unhandled exception caught during execution\cb1 \
\
\cb16 Error: At Expression [1] wrapper:14:16: AssertionError: condition was unexpectedly False\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Each function also accepts an optional 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 msg
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  keyword argument for providing a custom message to include if the assertion fails.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf17 \cb16 assert_true\cf5 (\cf19 False\cf5 ,\cf17  msg\cf5 =\cf23 "paradoxes are not allowed"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf20 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf21 \
