\fs28 \cf17 \cb16 Unhandled exception caught during execution\cb1 \
\
\cb16 Error: At Expression [3] wrapper:15:24: AssertionError: 3.3333333333333335 is not close to 3.3300000000000001 with a diff of 0.0033333333333334103 (close but no cigar)\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The testing module also defines a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/errors/#use-a-context-manager"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 context manager}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/testing/assert_raises/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 \ul \ulc5 assert_raises()}}, to assert that a given code block correctly raises an expected error.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb16 def\cf17  \cf18 inc\cf5 (\cf17 n\cf5 :\cf17  Int\cf5 )\cf17  raises \cf5 ->\cf17  Int\cf5 :\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     \cf5 if\cf17  n \cf5 ==\cf17  Int\cf5 .\cf17 MAX\cf5 :\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16          \cf5 raise\cf17  Error\cf5 (\cf23 "inc overflow"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     \cf5 return\cf17  n \cf5 +\cf17  \cf19 1\cf17 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 print(\cf23 "Test passes because the error is raised"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb16 with\cf17  assert_raises\cf5 ():\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     _ \cf5 =\cf17  inc\cf5 (\cf17 Int\cf5 .\cf17 MAX\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 print(\cf23 "Test fails because the error isn't raised"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb16 with\cf17  assert_raises\cf5 ():\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     _ \cf5 =\cf17  inc\cf5 (\cf17 Int\cf5 .\cf17 MIN\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

