\fs28 \cf2 \cb22 The example above assigns the return value from 
\fs24\fsmilli12250 \cf10 \cb14 inc()
\fs28 \cf2 \cb22  to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/lifecycle/death/#explicit-lifetime-extension"}}{\fldrslt \ul discard pattern}}. Without it, the Mojo compiler reports a warning that the return value is unused.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 You can also provide an optional 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 contains
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  argument to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 assert_raises()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  to indicate that the test passes only if the error message contains the substring specified. Other errors are propagated, failing the test.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb16 print(\cf23 "Test passes because the error contains the substring"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb16 with\cf17  assert_raises\cf5 (\cf17 contains\cf5 =\cf23 "required"\cf5 ):\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     \cf5 raise\cf17  Error\cf5 (\cf23 "missing required argument"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 print(\cf23 "Test fails because the error doesn't contain the substring"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb16 with\cf17  assert_raises\cf5 (\cf17 contains\cf5 =\cf23 "required"\cf5 ):\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     \cf5 raise\cf17  Error\cf5 (\cf23 "invalid value"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

