\fs64 \cf2 Writing unit tests\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 A Mojo unit test is simply a function that fulfills all of these requirements:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Has a name that starts with 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 test_
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  for automatic discovery.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Accepts no arguments.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Returns 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 None
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Raises an error to indicate test failure.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Is defined at the module scope, not as a Mojo struct method.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Generally, you should use the assertion utilities from the Mojo standard library {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/testing/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 \ul \ulc5 testing}} module to implement your tests. You can include multiple related assertions in the same test function. However, if an assertion raises an error during execution, then the test function returns immediately, skipping any subsequent assertions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa800\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 Running tests with TestSuite\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 To run your tests, each test file must include a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 main()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  function that uses {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/testing/suite/TestSuite/#discover_tests"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 \ul \ulc5 TestSuite.discover_tests()}} to automatically discover and execute all test functions in the module. The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 __functions_in_module()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  compiler intrinsic provides a list of all functions defined in the current module, which 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 discover_tests()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  filters to find those with the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 test_
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  prefix.\
Here is an example of a test file containing three tests for functions defined in a source module named 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb15 my_target_module
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  (which is not shown here).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf6 \cb16 # File: test_my_target_module.mojo\cf17 \cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb16 from\cf17  my_target_module \cf5 import\cf17  convert_input\cf5 ,\cf17  validate_input\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb16 from\cf17  std\cf5 .\cf17 testing \cf5 import\cf17  assert_equal\cf5 ,\cf17  assert_false\cf5 ,\cf17  assert_raises\cf5 ,\cf17  assert_true\cf5 ,\cf17  TestSuite\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 def\cf17  \cf18 test_validate_input\cf5 ()\cf17  raises\cf5 :\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     assert_true\cf5 (\cf17 validate_input\cf5 (\cf23 "good"\cf5 ),\cf17  msg\cf5 =\cf23 "'good' should be valid input"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     assert_false\cf5 (\cf17 validate_input\cf5 (\cf23 "bad"\cf5 ),\cf17  msg\cf5 =\cf23 "'bad' should be invalid input"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 def\cf17  \cf18 test_convert_input\cf5 ()\cf17  raises\cf5 :\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     assert_equal\cf5 (\cf17 convert_input\cf5 (\cf23 "input1"\cf5 ),\cf17  \cf23 "output1"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     assert_equal\cf5 (\cf17 convert_input\cf5 (\cf23 "input2"\cf5 ),\cf17  \cf23 "output2"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 def\cf17  \cf18 test_convert_input_error\cf5 ()\cf17  raises\cf5 :\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     \cf5 with\cf17  assert_raises\cf5 ():\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16         _ \cf5 =\cf17  convert_input\cf5 (\cf23 "garbage"\cf5 )\cf17 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb16 def\cf17  \cf18 main\cf5 ()\cf17  raises\cf5 :\cf17 \cb1 \
\cb16     TestSuite\cf5 .\cf17 discover_tests\cf5 [\cf17 __functions_in_module\cf5 ()]().\cf17 run\cf5 ()\cf17 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf20 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf21 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
